Z||000000||overlord||12-07-2000||12:05 AM||||was reading that other post about refinishing the tech-alloy wheels....so i went outside and grabbed my spare wheel and went to work on it...just one question.<P>What sort of  thing do you use to polish the wheel? I havnet a clue what a polishing wheel is (well i sort of do), but is it something that just attaches onto a drill, or is it a separate tool that i have to buy?<P>I really want to get these  wheels shiny.<P>I have a car  polisher but i dont think thats what is meant by "polishing disk".<P>I asked dad, he didnt know. I looked in the canadian tire book for some sort of polishing wheel, but nothing.....so what the heck is it?||||reg||1
Z||000001||DXR_DAD||12-07-2000||12:59 AM||||Lots of different info on wheel polishing and what to use and whats best. Try doing a search using polishing, wheel polish, etc.<BR>as a key word.<P>Here is one: <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/002549.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/002549.html</A> <P><BR>Hope this helps<BR>DXR_DAD||||reg||6
