Z||000003||Fformula88||12-07-2000||08:06 PM||||What you use will depend on how much polishing your wheel will need.  If its badly pitted or scratched, you are going to need something more abrasive.  You can buy metal polish (not necsessarily just for aluminum, but it will work) in different grades.  Get a few different grades and practice on your extra wheel.  The fine polishes will bring out a brilliant shine, where as the more coarse ones will not.  So if you use a coarser polish don't worry if it doesn't look mirror bright right away.  A good finishing polish is mothers aluminum wheel polish... you should be able to get it at an autoparts store.  ||||reg||1
