Z||000005||overlord||12-07-2000||10:25 PM||||well, the clearcoat is chipping and looks pretty bad on a couple of the wheels. I was going to buy aftermarket wheels and tires...but  probably neever afford it. So i read the post on "who has stripped their wheels"..and  thohgt it would be a hell of a lot chepaer to refinish the wheels.<P>So far on my extra wheel (i am doing half  of it just to see results), i have removed all the clearcoat (easier than i thoght) I used some sort of gel  paint remover and the clearcoat came off in a matter of seconds, so i left it 20 mins and it literally wiped off with a cloth.  And i have just begun sanding with sandpaper to get all the maching marks out....(I should  of bought more paper!!!)....And then i will polish. <P>Ill  post a pic after alls done If it looks good.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Raydar||12-07-2000||11:35 PM||||I polished my wheels, a while back. It's documented on Darklord's site (Fieroproject.com) under "modifications".<BR>Or click here...<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com/wheel.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com/wheel.htm</A> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/wheel_10.jpg"> <P><p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 12-07-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||overlord||12-12-2000||08:34 AM||||just finished final  polishing of part of my test wheel. OMG it looks beautiful.  Half the wheel i left and half a sanded and  polished,  i cant wait till i  get the other 4.5 wheels done!  If your wheels are corroding, clearcoat chiipping, then i recommend doing this.  It  is a lot of sanding and scrubbing but i just cant get over what a difference there is. Im going to get the fiero painted black too so itll look twice as good!<P>And so far ive  onlyu spent about 60$ canadaina for supplys.....hell of a lot cheaper than  new wheels.<BR>||||reg||1
